WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.850
When unit 3 is taken in
to Hachioji for an upgrade...

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:05.020
Asuma and Noa's relationship
takes a turn for the worse.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:11.060
Meanwhile, the Self Defense Force
stages war games in Oshima.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.610
But a mysterious Labor
intrudes on the action.

00:02:16.490 --> 00:02:23.120
Captain Goto, sensing a trap,
sends Asuma back for unit 3.

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:26.660
The rest of the team
heads for Oshima without Asuma.

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:33.790
Return of the Phantom

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:08.500
You're going to have a tough time
if you don't get some sleep.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:10.580
I know.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.430
That's it! Keep going.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.680
Start the diagnostics as soon
as the hardware is in place.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.270
Unit 3:
Are you ready for refitting?

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:32.690
Any time, sir.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:36.440
Begin fitting
the exterior components.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:37.520
Yes, sir!

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.190
It'll take another two hours.

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:43.530
After that, I can get you
to Inatori on a cargo ship...

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:47.740
A cargo ship? Don't tell me
my father ordered it.

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:51.660
Asuma, get off it, will you?

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:01.590
An unidentified Labor was
spotted this afternoon.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.260
Its purpose is unknown,
but it may be dangerous.

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:10.470
All residents must evacuate
to the town hall.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.020
I repeat...

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:28.160
The surveillance copter
reports that Block 6 is clear.

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.160
The question is:
Where will it show up?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:36.130
We aren't authorized to leave
the training grounds.

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:38.590
I don't think that'll be problem.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.630
The coast guard is
patrolling the area.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.180
HSS won't fight this thing.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:51.560
But our Labors could lure it onto
the training ground for you.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:52.560
I see.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:57.060
Sir, the Labor team in Narashino
wants permission for an air-drop.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:58.020
Not yet.

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.030
There's no point in dropping
until the enemy's mobilized.

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:18.500
The ocean's kind of creepy at night.

00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.100
- Quit startling me like that!
- Let's go home.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.770
- I won't criticize ya.
- Go ahead and leave!

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:34.270
All right, I will.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.480
But the boat stays here.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:38.850
I can't leave it behind!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.020
I'll get you
a couple bottles of sake.

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:43.650
Two sakes.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:44.900
No, thanks!

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.540
HSS, unit 2 here.
Target spotted.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:01.460
About to engage...

00:06:14.060 --> 00:06:16.060
- How's the pilot?
- He's okay.

00:06:16.560 --> 00:06:17.810
They've taken him to the hospital.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:20.270
So it's landed.

00:06:20.560 --> 00:06:21.310
But...

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:25.320
Excuse me,
I saw the whole thing!

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:29.700
The Labor that inflicted this damage
is heading straight for Sashiki!

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.620
I have a residual heat signature.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:35.660
It's advancing at 9 o'clock
headed toward Sashiki.

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:37.660
That's what
I just finished saying!

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.830
Move all the 97's to the south
of the training ground.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.130
And alert the HellDiver team.

00:06:44.550 --> 00:06:44.920
Roger.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.220
I'm heading back to the port.

00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:55.510
The Tokyo Police are coming
to assist the Coast Guard.

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.870
All right! Straight ahead!

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:21.920
Are you Kiichi Goto?

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:25.960
And you would be...?

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:28.380
Beg your pardon.

00:07:29.050 --> 00:07:33.760
I'm a negotiator of sorts, for Holly
Security Services' Labor division.

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.300
I see.

00:07:35.800 --> 00:07:39.220
A negotiator of sorts.
Interesting.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:44.980
- And you're here because...?
- I'll show you the coast guard.

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:46.860
Is that one of your regular services?

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:48.730
Actually,
I wanted to introduce myself.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.200
How charming;
I'm flattered.

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.240
Well, I'm afraid
we have work to do.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:57.950
Forgive me for staring.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:01.330
It's just that you remind me
of one of my superiors.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:06.290
You have a superior like me?
You certainly have my sympathy.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.170
- I'd better let you get to work.
- Right.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.140
One more thing.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.760
Have you seen this "mystery Labor?"

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.720
- No.
- Too bad.

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:24.810
I'd sure like to know who built it.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:27.860
But I guess you can't help me
if you haven't seen it.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.900
Sorry I couldn't be of help.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.700
Hiromi, are you okay?

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:40.200
I'm all right, but it still feels
like we're on the boat.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.960
What's with the queasy expression?

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.170
Buck up!

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.420
Easy for you to say;
you got some sleep!

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.130
And you didn't?

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:51.960
A good policeman
can sleep anywhere!

00:08:51.960 --> 00:08:55.340
A cop makes endurance
priority one and two!

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.930
- I dunno what priority three is!
- Listen up, people.

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.100
We're going to try
NOT to engage the enemy.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:05.810
We have an unspoken agreement
with the Self Defense Force.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:10.770
If we chase it onto their training
grounds, the JSDF will handle it.

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:11.860
Okey-dokey?

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.320
I can't do that; it's cowardly!

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:18.780
- Can't we just be happy, folks?
- Captain!

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:23.250
One question: Who's going to
command me in Alphonse?

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.210
Do you have any objection to me?

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.330
Not at all.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:34.380
But Mr. Jitsuyama, we won't
be able to use machine 3.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:39.260
Because it'll be useless without
an operating disk, you mean.

00:09:39.260 --> 00:09:41.140
- No problem!
- Shige!

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.480
The boss gave this to me.

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.560
Mr. Sakaki did?

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:52.110
A genuine copy of Alphonse's data.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:53.610
You know what that's like.

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:57.320
No, wait; I guess you don't know
what that's like.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:02.660
On the way here,
I heard an update on my radio.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.540
They've landed in Oshima,
and they expect combat tonight.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.290
Can I make it in time?

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.880
You'll manage somehow.

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:27.890
Three minutes to drop zone.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:31.810
Raven 1 to Raven 2 and 3:
Final check.

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.270
Where's our signal
from the ground team?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.980
Ground team: Come in!
Ground team! Ground team!

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:24.240
Kyumaira

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:31.370
Unit 2, deck up.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.170
- Ota, get ready to move out.
- Roger!

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:36.380
And so it begins.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:38.710
Captain, what should I do?

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.470
Pray that
it doesn't come this way.

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:42.470
Pardon?!

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.020
Raven 3, are you all right?

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:59.480
Yeah, but my knees are shot.
I can't move.

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:03.950
- Raven 2, let's go.
- Roger.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:14.830
Kanuka, beyond this point is
the JSDF training grounds.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:19.050
Do you see any roadblocks?
I sure don't.

00:12:19.250 --> 00:12:21.010
Neither do I!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.970
Come on guys,
the Captain's orders...

00:12:24.380 --> 00:12:29.680
To chase it onto the grounds,
we have to enter the grounds.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:33.770
If we surround the enemy,
we still have to trespass.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:36.560
- Yeah, but...
- Don't sweat the details.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.070
- Somebody has to!
- There's no point in worrying.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:51.200
Come in HQ!

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.620
A police Labor has
entered the training grounds!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:00.170
Here it comes!

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:05.680
Where's he hiding?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:07.640
Keep moving!

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:11.140
You can't beat his weapon;
you have to move into close range!

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.680
I can handle this!

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:24.860
I don't need a monitor!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:37.670
No good!

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.380
Gonna try
the same trick again?!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.010
Go ahead; just try it!

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:03.150
Surrender!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.110
Ota's pretty good.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:08.990
This is Ota's second try.
He has to use his brain sometime.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:12.200
Didn't our opponent
learn from last time too?

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:20.130
Those are the exact moves
that unit 1 used.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:21.250
You...

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.260
Ota!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:31.850
Over there!

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:16.720
Ota!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:19.350
Ota! Ota!

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.400
Wake up! Ota!

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:27.940
They're using the beam weapon
we saw at Tokyo Teleport.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:29.860
It's definitely the same people.

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:32.740
Well, Ota's out
of the action for now.

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.910
I suppose I should be glad he's safe.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:38.160
Don't forget to hand in
his operating disk.

00:15:38.160 --> 00:15:38.870
Roger.

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:43.580
Captain, how long
do I have to sit here?

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:44.750
You bored?

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.340
That's not what I meant.

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.550
Wait a little longer.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.340
For what?

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:52.970
For many things.

00:16:04.690 --> 00:16:05.610
I must have it.

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:12.990
It'd be a gold mine if I could get
my hands on unit 1's operating data.

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.070
Can the Phantom
close with unit 1?

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:21.250
Unit 1 is near civilians;
it's too risky.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:23.040
Besides, it's almost dawn.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.500
I don't care.
That data is more than worth it.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:53.450
Captain,
the training grounds end here.

00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:54.900
I know.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:56.780
- We can't advance...
- Silence!

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:18.550
He's here!

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:24.980
Where is he?

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:28.980
Sooner than I expected.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:33.070
Calm down, Izumi.
He's trying to draw you out.

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.820
Don't move an inch, got it?!

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:35.530
But sir...!

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.830
There'll be hell to pay!

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:44.370
Just follow orders.

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.620
Aim for the central head lens.

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:52.630
Captain, they need my help!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.550
Wait, Izumi!

00:17:55.970 --> 00:17:58.510
I swear, she has <i>no</i> patience.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.180
Are you certain?

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:07.020
Positive. There was
definitely a second Labor.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:09.650
I'm sure of it.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:25.790
Now!

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:56.990
We've lost the data feed!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.700
Recall the Phantom.
Send backup!

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.160
You saved me again.

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:03.830
Just returning the favor.

00:19:06.950 --> 00:19:08.710
- I'll get him!
- Wait!

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:13.420
Another Labor's there with a gun.
Be careful.

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:14.500
Roger!

00:19:16.170 --> 00:19:18.340
Division 2 is lucky to have her.

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:23.890
Kanuka!

00:19:26.180 --> 00:19:27.140
Did you find it?

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:52.080
You can't pull that again!

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:56.750
Creep!

00:20:05.350 --> 00:20:08.560
You're sure it was a 42mm shell?

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.980
Yes. I think it's from
the Saturn's auto-cannon.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:19.730
The security company!

00:20:25.070 --> 00:20:27.620
A Labor with a gun...?
It can't be!

00:20:38.420 --> 00:20:39.750
Did I miss anything, Noa?

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:41.840
Asuma!

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:48.390
Noa, catch!

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:52.310
This'll finish him off!

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.990
- I did it!
- Look out!

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:26.050
Asuma...

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.180
Thank you.

00:21:29.680 --> 00:21:30.470
You goof.

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:38.190
We've lost the Phantom's signal.
It might've been destroyed.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.570
Take us out of here.

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:54.500
That was quite
the little performance.

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:03.800
Izumi, think you can shoot
down that helicopter?

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:07.340
Just kidding. Get it?

00:22:16.310 --> 00:22:19.520
HSS says they've never
employed anyone named Kurosaki.

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:21.980
I figured as much.

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:26.530
So you don't think
this case is closed yet?

00:22:26.990 --> 00:22:28.910
It is for them.

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:35.290
Gimme a break!

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:45.380
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.510 --> 00:22:49.090
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:55.350
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:02.770 --> 00:23:04.860
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:04.980 --> 00:23:07.780
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:12.370
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.030 --> 00:23:17.040
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.120 --> 00:23:19.870
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:24.040
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.210 --> 00:23:30.550
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:35.810
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:38.350
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.350 --> 00:23:41.560
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:45.650
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.030 --> 00:23:51.820
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:57.870
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:04.500
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:09.210
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.000 --> 00:24:09.210
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:12.470 --> 00:24:15.260
The ways of the mafia world
can't be helped.

00:24:15.260 --> 00:24:17.510
Please don't try and
stop me sister.

00:24:17.510 --> 00:24:19.720
In the midst of
falling sakura blossoms...

00:24:19.720 --> 00:24:22.060
the hands grasping the lever
are crying.

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:23.810
The dons of Japan?

00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:27.650
A mafia boss runs off
with a collection of labors.

00:24:27.650 --> 00:24:31.900
Oh, the tattoo on this labor
is beautiful. It's amazing.

00:24:32.280 --> 00:24:36.280
